KG42.register("nodes-4a60c6e21872a2222cd0559d",{"id":"KG40-a6a3b767e2722b06","code":"PRD009.2","label":"Local electricity product with source-specific and operating-state restrictions","definition":"Electric energy traded among peers for purchase and sale within the local network; positive surplus eligibility and battery charge-discharge use are restricted by source and operating state.","layer":"L2","template_code":"CBA","concept_id":"product.local_energy","concept_ids":["product.local_energy"],"identity_dimensions":{"identity_fields":["Economic object: electric energy","Delivery content: peer-to-peer purchase and sale of electric energy","Quantity dimension: the quantity of electric energy defined by the source","Necessary scope: the local network and the product eligibility corresponding to the state"]},"exclusions":[["When E_{n,s}>0, tradable surplus exists, with quantity E_{n,s}.","The source is rooftop solar panels; the example prosumer is not equipped with a battery.","The scope is the coalition P2P network connected to the CPS."],["In state 1, a positive surplus E_{n,sur}(t)>0 is sold; Eq. (2): E_{n,sur}(t)=(E_{n,pv}(t)+E_{n,dis}(t))−(E_{n,hou}(t)+E_{n,cha}(t)).","In state 1, the battery does not charge or discharge for P2P trading; E_{n,dis} and E_{n,cha} are the household's own battery operations before trading and cannot be directly set to zero.","State 2 includes battery discharge energy e_{n,d}(t) sold to peers and energy e_{n,c}(t) purchased from peers for charging.","Differences in the surplus-shortage expression between the state-description paragraph and Eqs. (2)-(3) are retained according to their respective sources and are not uniformly rewritten."]],"members":[{"id":"30-motivational_game::v141-c-R007::V::product.local_energy","rule_id":"v141-c-R007","market_meaning":"The local energy product is surplus electricity from the prosumers' solar panels, traded among peers within the network. Scope: Illustrative canonical-coalition P2P network of rooftop-solar prosumers without batteries.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"bidding","context_text":"Illustrative canonical-coalition P2P network of rooftop-solar prosumers without batteries.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e05","v141-b-g02-e07"]},"constraint_refs":["30-motivational_game::v141-c-R007::v141-c-R007-C001","30-motivational_game::v141-c-R007::v141-c-R007-C002"],"decision_anchor":"product.local_energy","source_rule_sha256":"da22f62609d9d40b1660d09585edadecfd2c5b8050721e02f413e99e9147bd4c","paper":"30-motivational_game","rule_ref":"30-motivational_game::v141-c-R007","node_id":"product.local_energy","function":"product.local_energy","unit_id":"30-motivational_game::v141-a-M01::product.local_energy","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","anchor":true},{"id":"31-coalition_formation::v141-c-R008::V::product.local_energy","rule_id":"v141-c-R008","market_meaning":"The energy supplied for state-1 P2P trading is surplus generation. Scope: State-1 P2P trading in the considered prosumer network. Condition: The prosumer is in state 1, without charging or discharging its battery for P2P trading. The state-2 energy product includes energy discharged from batteries for sale to peers and energy purchased from peers for battery charging. Scope: State-2 P2P trading in the considered prosumer network. Condition: The prosumer is in state 2 and uses its battery for trading.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"bidding","context_text":"State-1 P2P trading in the considered prosumer network. | State-2 P2P trading in the considered prosumer network.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E003","v141-b-g01-E009"]},"constraint_refs":["31-coalition_formation::v141-c-R008::v141-c-R008-C001","31-coalition_formation::v141-c-R008::v141-c-R008-C002","31-coalition_formation::v141-c-R008::v141-c-R008-C003"],"decision_anchor":"product.local_energy","source_rule_sha256":"28233bf89e094e39c295e813aabe51304aef830dac57d0b3b659758a1f6102c7","paper":"31-coalition_formation","rule_ref":"31-coalition_formation::v141-c-R008","node_id":"product.local_energy","function":"product.local_energy","unit_id":"31-coalition_formation::v141-a-M01::product.local_energy","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","anchor":true}],"paper_ids":["30-motivational_game","31-coalition_formation"],"evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e05","location":{"location_id":"src-dd42379cd7-p06-c1r4__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":"3.2.2 Development of the trading scheme","anchor_text":"participate. th P2 3.2.2. Development of the trading scheme ps To use a canonical coalition game wit","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"To use a canonical coalition game with the above properties for designing a P2P trading scheme, it is assumed that a number of prosumers with rooftop solar panels (without batteries) are connected to a central power station (CPS). They are also connected to each other through a secure information system via their smart meters for all necessary communication and transactions of P2P trading. At any particular time, each prosumer n has a particular amount of electricity surplus E_{n,s} from the supply from its solar panel and deficiency E_{n,d}.","paper":"30-motivational_game","rule_id":"v141-c-R007","quote":"To use a canonical coalition game with the above properties for designing a P2P trading scheme, it is assumed that a number of prosumers with rooftop solar panels (without batteries) are connected to a central power station (CPS). They are also connected to each other through a secure information system via their smart meters for all necessary communication and transactions of P2P trading. At any particular time, each prosumer n has a particular amount of electricity surplus E_{n,s} from the supply from its solar panel and deficiency E_{n,d}."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e07","location":{"location_id":"src-dd42379cd7-p06-c2r1__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":"3.2.2 Development of the trading scheme","anchor_text":"Applied Energy 243 (2019) 10–20 Similarly, if there is any electricity deﬁciency, i.e., En , d > 0 ,","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"Similarly, if there is any electricity deficiency, i.e., E_{n,d} > 0, a prosumer first buys the necessary amount from the peers within the network and then from the CPS, if required. Thus, in P2P trading, all the prosumers cooperate with one another to trade the surplus energy among themselves as a first priority, and then interact with the grid, if necessary, to sell or buy the total excess or deficient energy respectively.","paper":"30-motivational_game","rule_id":"v141-c-R007","quote":"Similarly, if there is any electricity deficiency, i.e., E_{n,d} > 0, a prosumer first buys the necessary amount from the peers within the network and then from the CPS, if required. Thus, in P2P trading, all the prosumers cooperate with one another to trade the surplus energy among themselves as a first priority, and then interact with the grid, if necessary, to sell or buy the total excess or deficient energy respectively."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e06","location":{"location_id":"src-dd42379cd7-p06-c1r4__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":"3.2.2 Development of the trading scheme","anchor_text":"participate. th P2 3.2.2. Development of the trading scheme ps To use a canonical coalition game wit","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"If the prosumer has any surplus, i.e., E_{n,s} > 0, it sells it to meet the demand of other peers as the first priority and then to the CPS, if needed.","paper":"30-motivational_game","rule_id":"v141-c-R007","quote":"If the prosumer has any surplus, i.e., E_{n,s} > 0, it sells it to meet the demand of other peers as the first priority and then to the CPS, if needed."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E003","location":{"location_id":"src-e3722a409d-p02-c2r4__v141-a-M01-participation","page":2,"printed_page":null,"section":"1. Introduction","anchor_text":"al- prosumers. In particular, we use the framework of a cooperative game to [30] to capture the inte","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-02.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"State 1 refers to the state of a prosumer, in which it does not charge or discharge its battery for participating in P2P trading. It only uses its surplus generation for participating in the market. State 2 of a prosumer, on the other hand, refers to the state, in which it is willing to charge or discharge its battery for buying energy from or selling energy to the P2P market.","paper":"31-coalition_formation","rule_id":"v141-c-R008","quote":"State 1 refers to the state of a prosumer, in which it does not charge or discharge its battery for participating in P2P trading. It only uses its surplus generation for participating in the market. State 2 of a prosumer, on the other hand, refers to the state, in which it is willing to charge or discharge its battery for buying energy from or selling energy to the P2P market."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E007","location":{"location_id":"src-e3722a409d-p03-c2r2__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":"2. System model","anchor_text":"cordingly, d n,sur ( t ) = ( En ,pv (t ) + En,dis ( t )) ( En,hou ( t ) + En ,cha ( t )), (2) u- E a","equation_id":"2-3","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"Accordingly, based on the generation, demand, and consumption of energy, each prosumer n may need to buy excess energy to meet its energy deficiency E_{n,def}(t) or has surplus energy E_{n,sur}(t) to sell. Accordingly,\nE_{n,sur}(t) = (E_{n,pv}(t) + E_{n,dis}(t)) - (E_{n,hou}(t) + E_{n,cha}(t)), (2)\nand\nE_{n,def}(t) = (E_{n,hou}(t) + E_{n,cha}(t)) - (E_{n,pv}(t) + E_{n,dis}(t)). (3)","paper":"31-coalition_formation","rule_id":"v141-c-R008","quote":"Accordingly, based on the generation, demand, and consumption of energy, each prosumer n may need to buy excess energy to meet its energy deficiency E_{n,def}(t) or has surplus energy E_{n,sur}(t) to sell. Accordingly,\nE_{n,sur}(t) = (E_{n,pv}(t) + E_{n,dis}(t)) - (E_{n,hou}(t) + E_{n,cha}(t)), (2)\nand\nE_{n,def}(t) = (E_{n,hou}(t) + E_{n,cha}(t)) - (E_{n,pv}(t) + E_{n,dis}(t)). (3)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E009","location":{"location_id":"src-e3722a409d-p03-c2r3__v141-a-M01-participation","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":"2. System model","anchor_text":"a its battery in the energy trading market. Similarly, a state 1 prosumer in only buys energy, when ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":"Table 1","image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"We further consider that the prosumers participating in the P2P energy trading choose to be either of the two states at any given time slot t.\n(a) State 1 Prosumers in state 1 do not charge or discharge their batteries for trading purposes and only sell their surplus E_{n,sur}(t) to other prosumers in N\\{n\\} or to the grid when E_{n,sur}(t) = (E_{n,hou}(t) + E_{n,cha}(t)) - E_{n,pv}(t) > 0. In other words, a prosumer in state 1, which we denote as an element of set W, does not put its battery in the energy trading market. Similarly, a state 1 prosumer only buys energy, when necessary, to meet the deficient energy E_{n,def}(t) = (E_{n,pv}(t) + E_{n,dis}(t)) - E_{n,hou}(t). Note that a prosumer without any battery always remains in state 1.\n(b) State 2 Prosumers is state 2 use their batteries for trading purposes. That is, a prosumer in state 2, which we indicate via V is motivated, e.g., for more economical benefit, to discharge its battery for selling energy to other prosumers. Similarly, it may also buy energy from other peers to charge its battery for future needs.\nNote that when a prosumer does not have a battery (prosumer 6) or it does not want to charge or discharge despite having battery (prosumer 5 in time slot 1) will remain in state 1.","paper":"31-coalition_formation","rule_id":"v141-c-R008","quote":"We further consider that the prosumers participating in the P2P energy trading choose to be either of the two states at any given time slot t.\n(a) State 1 Prosumers in state 1 do not charge or discharge their batteries for trading purposes and only sell their surplus E_{n,sur}(t) to other prosumers in N\\{n\\} or to the grid when E_{n,sur}(t) = (E_{n,hou}(t) + E_{n,cha}(t)) - E_{n,pv}(t) > 0. In other words, a prosumer in state 1, which we denote as an element of set W, does not put its battery in the energy trading market. Similarly, a state 1 prosumer only buys energy, when necessary, to meet the deficient energy E_{n,def}(t) = (E_{n,pv}(t) + E_{n,dis}(t)) - E_{n,hou}(t). Note that a prosumer without any battery always remains in state 1.\n(b) State 2 Prosumers is state 2 use their batteries for trading purposes. That is, a prosumer in state 2, which we indicate via V is motivated, e.g., for more economical benefit, to discharge its battery for selling energy to other prosumers. Similarly, it may also buy energy from other peers to charge its battery for future needs.\nNote that when a prosumer does not have a battery (prosumer 6) or it does not want to charge or discharge despite having battery (prosumer 5 in time slot 1) will remain in state 1."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E011","location":{"location_id":"src-e3722a409d-p04-c1r4__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":"2.2 Utility of a prosumer at state 2","anchor_text":"thefact that the benefit to a prosumer for charging its battery even- wpr tually gets saturated with","equation_id":"5","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"We note that the utility that a prosumer obtains from charging its battery can be defined as the sum of the relevant cost and the benefit of charging. Benefit of charging can be captured by using a utility function with decreasing marginal benefit [34,44,45]. Such a property refers to the fact that the benefit to a prosumer for charging its battery eventually gets saturated with charging as the SoC s_n(t) of the battery becomes close to its available capacity b_{n,c}(t) = b_n - s_n(t).\nTo this end, we consider the utility of a state 2 prosumer n for charging its battery as:\nU_{n,c}(t) = k\\left[b_{n,c}(t)e_{n,c}(t) - \\frac{1}{2}\\alpha_n e_{n,c}(t)^2\\right] - (p_l + p_c(t))e_{n,c}(t). (5)\nIn (5), the term \\left(b_{n,c}(t)e_{n,c}(t) - \\frac{1}{2}\\alpha_n e_{n,c}(t)^2\\right) refers to the benefit of charging, 0 \u003c k \\le 1 is a scaling factor, and (p_l + p_c(t))e_{n,c}(t) is the cost of charging. Here, p_l is the degradation cost per kWh of the battery [46], p_c(t) is the price per unit of charging energy e_{n,c}(t) \\le E_{chr,dis} (where, E_{chr,dis} is the rated charging/discharging rate of the battery), and \\alpha_n > 0 is the satisfaction parameter of prosumer n [44].","paper":"31-coalition_formation","rule_id":"v141-c-R008","quote":"We note that the utility that a prosumer obtains from charging its battery can be defined as the sum of the relevant cost and the benefit of charging. Benefit of charging can be captured by using a utility function with decreasing marginal benefit [34,44,45]. Such a property refers to the fact that the benefit to a prosumer for charging its battery eventually gets saturated with charging as the SoC s_n(t) of the battery becomes close to its available capacity b_{n,c}(t) = b_n - s_n(t).\nTo this end, we consider the utility of a state 2 prosumer n for charging its battery as:\nU_{n,c}(t) = k\\left[b_{n,c}(t)e_{n,c}(t) - \\frac{1}{2}\\alpha_n e_{n,c}(t)^2\\right] - (p_l + p_c(t))e_{n,c}(t). (5)\nIn (5), the term \\left(b_{n,c}(t)e_{n,c}(t) - \\frac{1}{2}\\alpha_n e_{n,c}(t)^2\\right) refers to the benefit of charging, 0 \u003c k \\le 1 is a scaling factor, and (p_l + p_c(t))e_{n,c}(t) is the cost of charging. Here, p_l is the degradation cost per kWh of the battery [46], p_c(t) is the price per unit of charging energy e_{n,c}(t) \\le E_{chr,dis} (where, E_{chr,dis} is the rated charging/discharging rate of the battery), and \\alpha_n > 0 is the satisfaction parameter of prosumer n [44]."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E012","location":{"location_id":"src-e3722a409d-p04-c2r2__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":"2.2 Utility of a prosumer at state 2","anchor_text":"states by prosumer 1 and 2 from timeslot 1 to 2 Prosumer 3, 4, 5 and 6 remain in the same state in b","equation_id":"6-7","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"In the similar way, the utility of a state 2 prosumer n for discharging its battery can be defined as\nU_{n,d}(t) = k\\left[s_n(t)e_{n,d}(t) - \\frac{1}{2}\\alpha_n e_{n,d}(t)^2\\right] + (p_d(t) - p_l)e_{n,d}(t), (6)\nwhere p_d(t) is the price per unit of discharged energy e_{n,d}(t) \\le E_{chr,dis}. However, unlike (5), (p_d(t) - p_l)e_{n,d}(t) in (6) refers to the revenue that an n obtains from discharging its battery. Further,","paper":"31-coalition_formation","rule_id":"v141-c-R008","quote":"In the similar way, the utility of a state 2 prosumer n for discharging its battery can be defined as\nU_{n,d}(t) = k\\left[s_n(t)e_{n,d}(t) - \\frac{1}{2}\\alpha_n e_{n,d}(t)^2\\right] + (p_d(t) - p_l)e_{n,d}(t), (6)\nwhere p_d(t) is the price per unit of discharged energy e_{n,d}(t) \\le E_{chr,dis}. However, unlike (5), (p_d(t) - p_l)e_{n,d}(t) in (6) refers to the revenue that an n obtains from discharging its battery. Further,"}],"candidate_only":true,"classification_subtypes":["local_surplus_electricity","state_contingent_local_energy_product"],"projection_statuses":["clear"],"taxonomy":{"primary_family":"KG40-L2-SC-L2-df95af2bfabd6e15","secondary_families":[],"stage":"L2","ontological_kind":"SC-L2-df95af2bfabd6e15"},"semantic_definition":{"definition":"Electric energy traded among peers for purchase and sale within the local network; positive surplus eligibility and battery charge-discharge use are restricted by source and operating state.","identity_fields":["Economic object: electric energy","Delivery content: peer-to-peer purchase and sale of electric energy","Quantity dimension: the quantity of electric energy defined by the source","Necessary scope: the local network and the product eligibility corresponding to the state"]},"source_units":[{"unit_id":"30-motivational_game::v141-a-M01::product.local_energy","paper_id":"30-motivational_game","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","function":"product.local_energy","source_occurrences":[{"id":"30-motivational_game::v141-c-R007::V::product.local_energy","rule_id":"v141-c-R007","market_meaning":"The local energy product is surplus electricity from the prosumers' solar panels, traded among peers within the network. Scope: Illustrative canonical-coalition P2P network of rooftop-solar prosumers without batteries.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"bidding","context_text":"Illustrative canonical-coalition P2P network of rooftop-solar prosumers without batteries.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e05","v141-b-g02-e07"]},"constraint_refs":["30-motivational_game::v141-c-R007::v141-c-R007-C001","30-motivational_game::v141-c-R007::v141-c-R007-C002"],"decision_anchor":"product.local_energy","source_rule_sha256":"da22f62609d9d40b1660d09585edadecfd2c5b8050721e02f413e99e9147bd4c"}],"constraints":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R007-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The local energy product is surplus electricity from the prosumers' solar panels, traded among peers within the network. Scope: Illustrative canonical-coalition P2P network of rooftop-solar prosumers without batteries.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["product.local_energy"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e05","v141-b-g02-e07"],"ref":"30-motivational_game::v141-c-R007::v141-c-R007-C001","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R007","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e05","location":{"location_id":"src-dd42379cd7-p06-c1r4__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":"3.2.2 Development of the trading scheme","anchor_text":"participate. th P2 3.2.2. Development of the trading scheme ps To use a canonical coalition game wit","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"To use a canonical coalition game with the above properties for designing a P2P trading scheme, it is assumed that a number of prosumers with rooftop solar panels (without batteries) are connected to a central power station (CPS). They are also connected to each other through a secure information system via their smart meters for all necessary communication and transactions of P2P trading. At any particular time, each prosumer n has a particular amount of electricity surplus E_{n,s} from the supply from its solar panel and deficiency E_{n,d}."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e07","location":{"location_id":"src-dd42379cd7-p06-c2r1__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":"3.2.2 Development of the trading scheme","anchor_text":"Applied Energy 243 (2019) 10–20 Similarly, if there is any electricity deﬁciency, i.e., En , d > 0 ,","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"Similarly, if there is any electricity deficiency, i.e., E_{n,d} > 0, a prosumer first buys the necessary amount from the peers within the network and then from the CPS, if required. Thus, in P2P trading, all the prosumers cooperate with one another to trade the surplus energy among themselves as a first priority, and then interact with the grid, if necessary, to sell or buy the total excess or deficient energy respectively."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R007-C002","kind":"mathematical","role":"supporting","statement":"For each prosumer n, a positive solar-panel electricity surplus E_{n,s} > 0 is the condition under which the prosumer offers its surplus as the local energy product to other peers; the surplus amount is E_{n,s}.","expression":"E_{n,s} > 0","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["product.local_energy"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R007-theta-E_ns"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e05","v141-b-g02-e06","v141-b-g02-e07"],"ref":"30-motivational_game::v141-c-R007::v141-c-R007-C002","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R007","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e05","location":{"location_id":"src-dd42379cd7-p06-c1r4__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":"3.2.2 Development of the trading scheme","anchor_text":"participate. th P2 3.2.2. Development of the trading scheme ps To use a canonical coalition game wit","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"To use a canonical coalition game with the above properties for designing a P2P trading scheme, it is assumed that a number of prosumers with rooftop solar panels (without batteries) are connected to a central power station (CPS). They are also connected to each other through a secure information system via their smart meters for all necessary communication and transactions of P2P trading. At any particular time, each prosumer n has a particular amount of electricity surplus E_{n,s} from the supply from its solar panel and deficiency E_{n,d}."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e06","location":{"location_id":"src-dd42379cd7-p06-c1r4__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":"3.2.2 Development of the trading scheme","anchor_text":"participate. th P2 3.2.2. Development of the trading scheme ps To use a canonical coalition game wit","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"If the prosumer has any surplus, i.e., E_{n,s} > 0, it sells it to meet the demand of other peers as the first priority and then to the CPS, if needed."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e07","location":{"location_id":"src-dd42379cd7-p06-c2r1__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":"3.2.2 Development of the trading scheme","anchor_text":"Applied Energy 243 (2019) 10–20 Similarly, if there is any electricity deﬁciency, i.e., En , d > 0 ,","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"Similarly, if there is any electricity deficiency, i.e., E_{n,d} > 0, a prosumer first buys the necessary amount from the peers within the network and then from the CPS, if required. Thus, in P2P trading, all the prosumers cooperate with one another to trade the surplus energy among themselves as a first priority, and then interact with the grid, if necessary, to sell or buy the total excess or deficient energy respectively."}]}],"variables":[],"parameters":[{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R007-theta-E_ns","symbol":"E_{n,s}","meaning":"Electricity surplus of prosumer n from the supply from its solar panel; this surplus is the local energy product traded among peers within the P2P network.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":null,"indices":["n"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e05","v141-b-g02-e06","v141-b-g02-e07"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R007","declaration_ref":"30-motivational_game::v141-c-R007::theta::v141-c-R007-theta-E_ns"}]},{"unit_id":"31-coalition_formation::v141-a-M01::product.local_energy","paper_id":"31-coalition_formation","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","function":"product.local_energy","source_occurrences":[{"id":"31-coalition_formation::v141-c-R008::V::product.local_energy","rule_id":"v141-c-R008","market_meaning":"The energy supplied for state-1 P2P trading is surplus generation. Scope: State-1 P2P trading in the considered prosumer network. Condition: The prosumer is in state 1, without charging or discharging its battery for P2P trading. The state-2 energy product includes energy discharged from batteries for sale to peers and energy purchased from peers for battery charging. Scope: State-2 P2P trading in the considered prosumer network. Condition: The prosumer is in state 2 and uses its battery for trading.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"bidding","context_text":"State-1 P2P trading in the considered prosumer network. | State-2 P2P trading in the considered prosumer network.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E003","v141-b-g01-E009"]},"constraint_refs":["31-coalition_formation::v141-c-R008::v141-c-R008-C001","31-coalition_formation::v141-c-R008::v141-c-R008-C002","31-coalition_formation::v141-c-R008::v141-c-R008-C003"],"decision_anchor":"product.local_energy","source_rule_sha256":"28233bf89e094e39c295e813aabe51304aef830dac57d0b3b659758a1f6102c7"}],"constraints":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R008-C001","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"The energy supplied for state-1 P2P trading is surplus generation. Scope: State-1 P2P trading in the considered prosumer network. Condition: The prosumer is in state 1, without charging or discharging its battery for P2P trading.","expression":"E_{n,sur}(t) = (E_{n,pv}(t) + E_{n,dis}(t)) - (E_{n,hou}(t) + E_{n,cha}(t))","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["product.local_energy"],"variable_refs":["x_E_sur","x_E_dis","x_E_cha"],"parameter_refs":["theta_E_pv","theta_E_hou"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E003","v141-b-g01-E007"],"ref":"31-coalition_formation::v141-c-R008::v141-c-R008-C001","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R008","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E003","location":{"location_id":"src-e3722a409d-p02-c2r4__v141-a-M01-participation","page":2,"printed_page":null,"section":"1. Introduction","anchor_text":"al- prosumers. In particular, we use the framework of a cooperative game to [30] to capture the inte","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-02.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"State 1 refers to the state of a prosumer, in which it does not charge or discharge its battery for participating in P2P trading. It only uses its surplus generation for participating in the market. State 2 of a prosumer, on the other hand, refers to the state, in which it is willing to charge or discharge its battery for buying energy from or selling energy to the P2P market."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E007","location":{"location_id":"src-e3722a409d-p03-c2r2__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":"2. System model","anchor_text":"cordingly, d n,sur ( t ) = ( En ,pv (t ) + En,dis ( t )) ( En,hou ( t ) + En ,cha ( t )), (2) u- E a","equation_id":"2-3","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"Accordingly, based on the generation, demand, and consumption of energy, each prosumer n may need to buy excess energy to meet its energy deficiency E_{n,def}(t) or has surplus energy E_{n,sur}(t) to sell. Accordingly,\nE_{n,sur}(t) = (E_{n,pv}(t) + E_{n,dis}(t)) - (E_{n,hou}(t) + E_{n,cha}(t)), (2)\nand\nE_{n,def}(t) = (E_{n,hou}(t) + E_{n,cha}(t)) - (E_{n,pv}(t) + E_{n,dis}(t)). (3)"}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R008-C002","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"The state-2 energy product includes energy discharged from batteries for sale to peers and energy purchased from peers for battery charging. Scope: State-2 P2P trading in the considered prosumer network. Condition: The prosumer is in state 2 and uses its battery for trading.","expression":"\\{e_{n,d}(t)\\ \\text{(battery energy discharged for sale to peers)},\\ e_{n,c}(t)\\ \\text{(energy purchased from peers for battery charging)}\\}","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["product.local_energy"],"variable_refs":["x_e_d","x_e_c"],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E009","v141-b-g01-E011","v141-b-g01-E012"],"ref":"31-coalition_formation::v141-c-R008::v141-c-R008-C002","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R008","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E009","location":{"location_id":"src-e3722a409d-p03-c2r3__v141-a-M01-participation","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":"2. System model","anchor_text":"a its battery in the energy trading market. Similarly, a state 1 prosumer in only buys energy, when ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":"Table 1","image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"We further consider that the prosumers participating in the P2P energy trading choose to be either of the two states at any given time slot t.\n(a) State 1 Prosumers in state 1 do not charge or discharge their batteries for trading purposes and only sell their surplus E_{n,sur}(t) to other prosumers in N\\{n\\} or to the grid when E_{n,sur}(t) = (E_{n,hou}(t) + E_{n,cha}(t)) - E_{n,pv}(t) > 0. In other words, a prosumer in state 1, which we denote as an element of set W, does not put its battery in the energy trading market. Similarly, a state 1 prosumer only buys energy, when necessary, to meet the deficient energy E_{n,def}(t) = (E_{n,pv}(t) + E_{n,dis}(t)) - E_{n,hou}(t). Note that a prosumer without any battery always remains in state 1.\n(b) State 2 Prosumers is state 2 use their batteries for trading purposes. That is, a prosumer in state 2, which we indicate via V is motivated, e.g., for more economical benefit, to discharge its battery for selling energy to other prosumers. Similarly, it may also buy energy from other peers to charge its battery for future needs.\nNote that when a prosumer does not have a battery (prosumer 6) or it does not want to charge or discharge despite having battery (prosumer 5 in time slot 1) will remain in state 1."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E011","location":{"location_id":"src-e3722a409d-p04-c1r4__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":"2.2 Utility of a prosumer at state 2","anchor_text":"thefact that the benefit to a prosumer for charging its battery even- wpr tually gets saturated with","equation_id":"5","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"We note that the utility that a prosumer obtains from charging its battery can be defined as the sum of the relevant cost and the benefit of charging. Benefit of charging can be captured by using a utility function with decreasing marginal benefit [34,44,45]. Such a property refers to the fact that the benefit to a prosumer for charging its battery eventually gets saturated with charging as the SoC s_n(t) of the battery becomes close to its available capacity b_{n,c}(t) = b_n - s_n(t).\nTo this end, we consider the utility of a state 2 prosumer n for charging its battery as:\nU_{n,c}(t) = k\\left[b_{n,c}(t)e_{n,c}(t) - \\frac{1}{2}\\alpha_n e_{n,c}(t)^2\\right] - (p_l + p_c(t))e_{n,c}(t). (5)\nIn (5), the term \\left(b_{n,c}(t)e_{n,c}(t) - \\frac{1}{2}\\alpha_n e_{n,c}(t)^2\\right) refers to the benefit of charging, 0 \u003c k \\le 1 is a scaling factor, and (p_l + p_c(t))e_{n,c}(t) is the cost of charging. Here, p_l is the degradation cost per kWh of the battery [46], p_c(t) is the price per unit of charging energy e_{n,c}(t) \\le E_{chr,dis} (where, E_{chr,dis} is the rated charging/discharging rate of the battery), and \\alpha_n > 0 is the satisfaction parameter of prosumer n [44]."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E012","location":{"location_id":"src-e3722a409d-p04-c2r2__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":"2.2 Utility of a prosumer at state 2","anchor_text":"states by prosumer 1 and 2 from timeslot 1 to 2 Prosumer 3, 4, 5 and 6 remain in the same state in b","equation_id":"6-7","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"In the similar way, the utility of a state 2 prosumer n for discharging its battery can be defined as\nU_{n,d}(t) = k\\left[s_n(t)e_{n,d}(t) - \\frac{1}{2}\\alpha_n e_{n,d}(t)^2\\right] + (p_d(t) - p_l)e_{n,d}(t), (6)\nwhere p_d(t) is the price per unit of discharged energy e_{n,d}(t) \\le E_{chr,dis}. However, unlike (5), (p_d(t) - p_l)e_{n,d}(t) in (6) refers to the revenue that an n obtains from discharging its battery. Further,"}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R008-C003","kind":"mathematical","role":"supporting","statement":"A state-1 prosumer sells surplus generation only when its surplus energy is positive.","expression":"E_{n,sur}(t) > 0","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["product.local_energy"],"variable_refs":["x_E_sur"],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E009"],"ref":"31-coalition_formation::v141-c-R008::v141-c-R008-C003","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R008","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E009","location":{"location_id":"src-e3722a409d-p03-c2r3__v141-a-M01-participation","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":"2. System model","anchor_text":"a its battery in the energy trading market. Similarly, a state 1 prosumer in only buys energy, when ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":"Table 1","image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"We further consider that the prosumers participating in the P2P energy trading choose to be either of the two states at any given time slot t.\n(a) State 1 Prosumers in state 1 do not charge or discharge their batteries for trading purposes and only sell their surplus E_{n,sur}(t) to other prosumers in N\\{n\\} or to the grid when E_{n,sur}(t) = (E_{n,hou}(t) + E_{n,cha}(t)) - E_{n,pv}(t) > 0. In other words, a prosumer in state 1, which we denote as an element of set W, does not put its battery in the energy trading market. Similarly, a state 1 prosumer only buys energy, when necessary, to meet the deficient energy E_{n,def}(t) = (E_{n,pv}(t) + E_{n,dis}(t)) - E_{n,hou}(t). Note that a prosumer without any battery always remains in state 1.\n(b) State 2 Prosumers is state 2 use their batteries for trading purposes. That is, a prosumer in state 2, which we indicate via V is motivated, e.g., for more economical benefit, to discharge its battery for selling energy to other prosumers. Similarly, it may also buy energy from other peers to charge its battery for future needs.\nNote that when a prosumer does not have a battery (prosumer 6) or it does not want to charge or discharge despite having battery (prosumer 5 in time slot 1) will remain in state 1."}]}],"variables":[{"variable_id":"x_E_sur","symbol":"E_{n,sur}(t)","meaning":"Energy surplus of prosumer n at time slot t; in state 1 this is the energy product offered to peers when positive.","kind":"operational","domain":"Time-indexed energy surplus quantity defined by Eq. (2); source gives no separate numerical bound for this surplus variable in the supplied definition.","unit":null,"indices":["n","t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E003","v141-b-g01-E007","v141-b-g01-E009"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R008","declaration_ref":"31-coalition_formation::v141-c-R008::x::x_E_sur"},{"variable_id":"x_E_dis","symbol":"E_{n,dis}(t)","meaning":"Energy discharged from prosumer n's battery at time slot t for its own/household operation before P2P market participation.","kind":"operational","domain":"Energy quantity; source defines it in the system model and uses it in the surplus/deficiency definitions. The state-1 P2P battery contribution is separately stated to be zero.","unit":null,"indices":["n","t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E006","v141-b-g01-E007","v141-b-g01-E010"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R008","declaration_ref":"31-coalition_formation::v141-c-R008::x::x_E_dis"},{"variable_id":"x_E_cha","symbol":"E_{n,cha}(t)","meaning":"Energy charged to prosumer n's battery at time slot t for its own operation before P2P market participation.","kind":"operational","domain":"Energy quantity; source defines it as part of demand and uses it in the surplus/deficiency definitions.","unit":null,"indices":["n","t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E006","v141-b-g01-E007"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R008","declaration_ref":"31-coalition_formation::v141-c-R008::x::x_E_cha"},{"variable_id":"x_e_c","symbol":"e_{n,c}(t)","meaning":"Energy charged by prosumer n's battery at time slot t; in state 2 it represents energy purchased from peers for battery charging.","kind":"operational","domain":"Energy quantity; source states e_{n,c}(t) \u003c= E_{chr,dis} and also bounds it in (7).","unit":null,"indices":["n","t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E009","v141-b-g01-E011","v141-b-g01-E013"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R008","declaration_ref":"31-coalition_formation::v141-c-R008::x::x_e_c"},{"variable_id":"x_e_d","symbol":"e_{n,d}(t)","meaning":"Energy discharged by prosumer n's battery at time slot t; in state 2 it represents battery energy sold to peers.","kind":"operational","domain":"Energy quantity; source states e_{n,d}(t) \u003c= E_{chr,dis} and also bounds it in (7).","unit":null,"indices":["n","t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E009","v141-b-g01-E012","v141-b-g01-E013"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R008","declaration_ref":"31-coalition_formation::v141-c-R008::x::x_e_d"}],"parameters":[{"parameter_id":"theta_E_pv","symbol":"E_{n,pv}(t)","meaning":"Solar generation of prosumer n at time slot t, treated as an exogenous time-indexed input in the surplus definition.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":null,"indices":["n","t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E006","v141-b-g01-E007"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R008","declaration_ref":"31-coalition_formation::v141-c-R008::theta::theta_E_pv"},{"parameter_id":"theta_E_hou","symbol":"E_{n,hou}(t)","meaning":"Household energy demand of prosumer n at time slot t, treated as an exogenous time-indexed input in the surplus definition.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":null,"indices":["n","t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E006","v141-b-g01-E007"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R008","declaration_ref":"31-coalition_formation::v141-c-R008::theta::theta_E_hou"}]}],"source_definitions":[{"unit_id":"30-motivational_game::v141-a-M01::product.local_energy","stage":"L2","subtype":"local_surplus_electricity","projection_status":"clear","target_definition":"The local product is surplus electric energy generated by the prosumer's solar panels and supplied for peer trading within the network; when E_{n,s}>0, a surplus product is available, with quantity E_{n,s}.","form_kind":"conceptual","identity_fields":["Object: surplus electric energy of the prosumer","Product boundary: positive surplus and used for peer trading within the same network","Quantity representation: E_{n,s}"],"variation_fields":["Energy comes from rooftop solar panels","The example prosumer is not equipped with a battery","The scenario is a coalition P2P network connected to the CPS"],"constraint_refs":["30-motivational_game::v141-c-R007::v141-c-R007-C001","30-motivational_game::v141-c-R007::v141-c-R007-C002"],"paper_id":"30-motivational_game","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","function":"product.local_energy","template_code":"CBA"},{"unit_id":"31-coalition_formation::v141-a-M01::product.local_energy","stage":"L2","subtype":"state_contingent_local_energy_product","projection_status":"clear","target_definition":"The trading object is local electric energy distinguished by battery use: in state 1, a positive surplus E_{n,sur}(t)>0 is sold, and Eq. (2) is E_{n,sur}(t)=(E_{n,pv}(t)+E_{n,dis}(t))−(E_{n,hou}(t)+E_{n,cha}(t)); in state 2, the product includes battery discharge energy e_{n,d}(t) sold to peers and energy e_{n,c}(t) purchased from peers for charging.","form_kind":"conceptual","identity_fields":["Object: electric energy traded between peers","Core boundary: residual generation after non-trading battery use, versus battery charge-discharge energy used specifically for trading","Product predicate: positive surplus in state 1, or outward discharge and purchased charging energy in state 2"],"variation_fields":["In state 1, the battery does not charge or discharge for P2P trading","E_{n,dis} and E_{n,cha} represent the household's own battery operations before trading and cannot be directly set to zero","State 2 distinguishes two directions: battery energy sold and charging energy purchased","The surplus-shortage expression in the state-description paragraph differs from that in Eqs. (2)-(3); each is retained according to its source and not uniformly rewritten"],"constraint_refs":["31-coalition_formation::v141-c-R008::v141-c-R008-C001","31-coalition_formation::v141-c-R008::v141-c-R008-C002","31-coalition_formation::v141-c-R008::v141-c-R008-C003"],"paper_id":"31-coalition_formation","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","function":"product.local_energy","template_code":"CBA"}],"source_variants":[{"unit_id":"30-motivational_game::v141-a-M01::product.local_energy","retained_variants":["When E_{n,s}>0, tradable surplus exists, with quantity E_{n,s}.","The source is rooftop solar panels; the example prosumer is not equipped with a battery.","The scope is the coalition P2P network connected to the CPS."],"evidence_refs":["30-motivational_game::v141-a-M01::product.local_energy::projection"]},{"unit_id":"31-coalition_formation::v141-a-M01::product.local_energy","retained_variants":["In state 1, a positive surplus E_{n,sur}(t)>0 is sold; Eq. (2): E_{n,sur}(t)=(E_{n,pv}(t)+E_{n,dis}(t))−(E_{n,hou}(t)+E_{n,cha}(t)).","In state 1, the battery does not charge or discharge for P2P trading; E_{n,dis} and E_{n,cha} are the household's own battery operations before trading and cannot be directly set to zero.","State 2 includes battery discharge energy e_{n,d}(t) sold to peers and energy e_{n,c}(t) purchased from peers for charging.","Differences in the surplus-shortage expression between the state-description paragraph and Eqs. (2)-(3) are retained according to their respective sources and are not uniformly rewritten."],"evidence_refs":["31-coalition_formation::v141-a-M01::product.local_energy::projection"]}],"functional":{"is_child":true,"subdivision_pending":false,"baseline_parent_id":"COMP-145bffca1ff2da73","baseline_parent_code":"PRD009","secondary_class":"SC-L2-df95af2bfabd6e15","category":{"id":"SC-L2-df95af2bfabd6e15","stage":"L2","label_zh":"Local electric energy commodity","definition_zh":"An electric energy commodity used for electricity supply and use exchange within a defined community or distribution market scope; internal exchange restrictions, external market interfaces and supply eligibility are separately defined by each source.","main_identity_axes":["Economic object: electric energy commodity","Delivery content: electric energy exchange that meets electricity supply and demand","Quantity dimension: distinguish energy and power representations according to source, without default conversion","Necessary scope: a defined local trading boundary and its external interface"],"inclusion_criteria":["The source explicitly treats electric energy as an object of purchase and sale, sharing or supply","Has a defined community or distribution market trading scope","Source, surplus eligibility, use, time period and quantity representation can be fully retained as conditional branches"],"exclusion_criteria":["Products that explicitly use active power itself as the clearing object","Different delivery objects such as reactive power and reserves","An overall product identity that includes a mixed energy scope with heat cannot be directly regarded as a pure electric energy commodity"],"supporting_unit_ids":["01-central_pool::v141-a-M01::product.local_energy","04-energy_collectives::v141-a-M01::product.local_energy","19-two_stage_battery_sharing::v141-a-M01::product.local_energy","23-hierarchical_market_structure::v141-a-M01::product.local_energy","05-double_auction::v141-a-M01::product.local_energy","02-dlmp::v141-a-M01::product.local_energy","10-hierarchical_coordination::v141-a-M01::product.local_energy"],"status":"agent_defined_structurally_validated"},"definition":{"definition_zh":"Electric energy traded among peers for purchase and sale within the local network; positive surplus eligibility and battery charge-discharge use are restricted by source and operating state.","identity_fields":["Economic object: electric energy","Delivery content: peer-to-peer purchase and sale of electric energy","Quantity dimension: the quantity of electric energy defined by the source","Necessary scope: the local network and the product eligibility corresponding to the state"],"member_unit_ids":["30-motivational_game::v141-a-M01::product.local_energy","31-coalition_formation::v141-a-M01::product.local_energy"]}},"canonical_pointer":"/nodes/17"});
